  "question": {
    "text": "If the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> passes through the intersection of two mutually perpendicular planes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;and intercepts a unit length on positive <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis, then the intercept made by the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis is"
  },
